§ `reg 3(1) Terms defined here`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- “appropriate body”
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:15 | “appropriate body” means any body which regulates or is representative of any trade, profession, business or employment carried on by a relevant person;
@ref reg 3(1) "appropriate body" (src:15)
GIVEN `the body regulates any trade, profession, business or employment carried on by a relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is representative of any trade, profession, business or employment carried on by a relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 3(1) the body is an appropriate body` MEANS
    IF `the body regulates any trade, profession, business or employment carried on by a relevant person` OR `the body is representative of any trade, profession, business or employment carried on by a relevant person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any body which regulates or is representative of any trade, profession, business or employment carried on by a relevant person"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- “authorised cryptoasset firm” and “authorised person”
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- "authorised person" is a borrowed term (FSMA): the fact is asked as a BOOLEAN.
-- src:20 | “authorised person” means a person who is authorised for the purposes of FSMA;
@ref reg 3(1) "authorised person" (src:20)
GIVEN `the person is authorised for the purposes of FSMA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 3(1) the person is an authorised person` MEANS
    IF `the person is authorised for the purposes of FSMA`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a person who is authorised for the purposes of FSMA"

-- src:19 | “authorised cryptoasset firm” means an authorised person who is authorised to carry on a regulated activity specified by Chapter 2B (cryptoassets) of Part 2 (specified activities) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001;
@ref reg 3(1) "authorised cryptoasset firm" (src:19)
GIVEN `the person is an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorised to carry on a regulated activity specified by Chapter 2B (cryptoassets) of Part 2 (specified activities) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 3(1) the person is an authorised cryptoasset firm` MEANS
    IF `the person is an authorised person` AND `the person is authorised to carry on a regulated activity specified by Chapter 2B (cryptoassets) of Part 2 (specified activities) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an authorised person who is authorised to carry on a regulated activity specified by Chapter 2B (cryptoassets)"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- “beneficial owner”: the three-way pointer.  Regs 5 and 6 below give the meanings.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- A listed company is sent to reg 5 by the pointer, and reg 5(1) is silent for it (see the
-- fork register: "A listed company").  A corporation sole, an unincorporated association and
-- another legal entity are "any other case" and go to reg 6(9) (and see reg 6(7), fork
-- "6(7) against 6(9)").
-- src:22 | “beneficial owner”—
-- src:23 | in the case of a body corporate or partnership, has the meaning given by regulation 5;
-- src:24 | in the case of a trust or similar arrangement, or the estate of a deceased person in the course of administration, has the meaning given by regulation 6;
-- src:25 | in any other case, has the meaning given by regulation 6(9);
@ref reg 3(1) "beneficial owner" (src:22-25)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of customer`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`reg 3(1) beneficial owner is given by` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `a company` THEN LIST "regulation 5"
    WHEN `a limited liability partnership` THEN LIST "regulation 5"
    WHEN `a body corporate of another kind` THEN LIST "regulation 5"
    WHEN `a partnership other than a limited liability partnership` THEN LIST "regulation 5"
    WHEN `a trust` THEN LIST "regulation 6"
    WHEN `a foundation or other legal arrangement similar to a trust` THEN LIST "regulation 6"
    WHEN `the estate of a deceased person in the course of administration` THEN LIST "regulation 6"
    WHEN `an individual` THEN LIST "regulation 6(9)"
    WHEN `a corporation sole` THEN LIST "regulation 6(9)"
    WHEN `an unincorporated association` THEN LIST "regulation 6(9)"
    WHEN `another legal entity or legal arrangement` THEN LIST "regulation 6(9)"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- “body corporate”: includes two limbs, does not include two others
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:26 | “body corporate”—
-- src:27 | includes—
-- src:28 | a body corporate incorporated under the laws of the United Kingdom or any part of the United Kingdom, and
-- src:29 | a body corporate constituted under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom;
-- src:30 | but does not include—
-- src:31 | a corporation sole, or
-- src:32 | a partnership that, whether or not a legal person, is not regarded as a body corporate under the law by which it is governed;
@ref reg 3(1) "body corporate" (src:26-32)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of customer`
      `a partnership is regarded as a body corporate under the law by which it is governed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 3(1) the entity is a body corporate` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `a company` THEN JUST TRUE -- "includes a body corporate incorporated under the laws of the United Kingdom or any part of the United Kingdom, and a body corporate constituted under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom" (either place is covered)
    WHEN `a limited liability partnership` THEN JUST TRUE -- the same two limbs: a limited liability partnership is a body corporate (reg 5(2)(a) treats it as one)
    WHEN `a body corporate of another kind` THEN JUST TRUE -- the same two limbs
    WHEN `a corporation sole` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include a corporation sole"
    WHEN `a partnership other than a limited liability partnership` THEN
        IF `a partnership is regarded as a body corporate under the law by which it is governed`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the second exclusion is limited to a partnership "not regarded as a body corporate under the law by which it is governed", and the text does not say a partnership that IS so regarded is included
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include ... a partnership that, whether or not a legal person, is not regarded as a body corporate under the law by which it is governed"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the definition "includes" two limbs and excludes two; it does not close the list

