GIVEN `the regulation number` IS A NUMBER
      `the measures are relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 3(1) the measures required by a regulation are customer due diligence measures` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the regulation number` EQUALS 28 THEN JUST TRUE -- "the measures required by regulation 28"
        IF `the regulation number` EQUALS 29 THEN IF `the measures are relevant` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where relevant, those required by regulations 29 and 33 to 37"
        IF `the regulation number` AT LEAST 33 AND `the regulation number` AT MOST 37 THEN IF `the measures are relevant` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where relevant, those required by regulations 29 and 33 to 37"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means the measures required by regulation 28, and where relevant, those required by regulations 29 and 33 to 37"

-- src:62 | “enhanced customer due diligence measures” means the customer due diligence measures required under regulations 33 to 35;
