-- src:67 | “firm” means any entity that, whether or not a legal person, is not an individual and includes a body corporate and a partnership or other unincorporated association;
@ref reg 3(1) "firm" (src:67)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of customer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 3(1) the entity is a firm` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `an individual` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any entity that ... is not an individual"
    WHEN `a company` THEN JUST TRUE -- "includes a body corporate"
    WHEN `a limited liability partnership` THEN JUST TRUE -- "includes a body corporate and a partnership"
    WHEN `a body corporate of another kind` THEN JUST TRUE -- "includes a body corporate"
    WHEN `a partnership other than a limited liability partnership` THEN JUST TRUE -- "includes ... a partnership"
    WHEN `an unincorporated association` THEN JUST TRUE -- "includes ... other unincorporated association"
    WHEN `a corporation sole` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether a corporation sole is an "entity" is not said
    WHEN `a trust` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether a trust is an "entity" is not said
    WHEN `a foundation or other legal arrangement similar to a trust` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "entity"
    WHEN `the estate of a deceased person in the course of administration` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "entity"
    WHEN `another legal entity or legal arrangement` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "entity"

