DECLARE `reg 3(1) Place of a market` IS ONE OF
    `within the United Kingdom`
    `within the EEA`
    `outside the EEA`

-- src:102 | “regulated market”—
-- src:103 | within the United Kingdom, means a UK regulated market, as defined by Article 2(1)(13A) of the markets in financial instruments regulation; and
-- src:104 | outside the United Kingdom, means—
-- src:105 | within the EEA, an EU regulated market, as defined by Article 2(1)(13B) of the markets in financial instruments regulation; or
-- src:106 | outside the EEA, a regulated financial market which subjects companies whose securities are admitted to trading to disclosure obligations which are equivalent to the specified disclosure obligations;
@ref reg 3(1) "regulated market" (src:102-106)
GIVEN place IS A `reg 3(1) Place of a market`
      `the market is a UK regulated market, as defined by Article 2(1)(13A) of the markets in financial instruments regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the market is an EU regulated market, as defined by Article 2(1)(13B) of the markets in financial instruments regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the market is a regulated financial market which subjects companies whose securities are admitted to trading to disclosure obligations equivalent to the specified disclosure obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 3(1) the market is a regulated market` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `within the United Kingdom` THEN
        IF `the market is a UK regulated market, as defined by Article 2(1)(13A) of the markets in financial instruments regulation`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within the United Kingdom, means a UK regulated market, as defined by Article 2(1)(13A)"
    WHEN `within the EEA` THEN
        IF `the market is an EU regulated market, as defined by Article 2(1)(13B) of the markets in financial instruments regulation`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "outside the United Kingdom, means— within the EEA, an EU regulated market"
    WHEN `outside the EEA` THEN
        IF `the market is a regulated financial market which subjects companies whose securities are admitted to trading to disclosure obligations equivalent to the specified disclosure obligations`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "outside the EEA, a regulated financial market which subjects companies whose securities are admitted to trading to disclosure obligations which are equivalent to the specified disclosure obligations"

