GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
`reg 3(1) the provisions that name the supervisory authority` MEANS
    IF `the person is a relevant person` AND `the person is a payment service provider`
    THEN JUST (LIST "regulation 7", "the transfer of funds supervisory authority")
    ELSE IF `the person is a relevant person`
        THEN JUST (LIST "regulation 7")
        ELSE IF `the person is a payment service provider`
            THEN JUST (LIST "the transfer of funds supervisory authority")
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the definition names a supervisory authority only "in relation to" a relevant person or a payment service provider

-- src:125 | “supervisory functions” means the functions given to a supervisory authority under these Regulations;
@ref reg 3(1) "supervisory functions" (src:125)
GIVEN `the function is given to a supervisory authority under these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 3(1) the function is a supervisory function` MEANS
    IF `the function is given to a supervisory authority under these Regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means the functions given to a supervisory authority under these Regulations"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- “terrorist financing”: a closed list of offences, unless the context otherwise requires
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DECLARE `reg 3(1) Offence an act may constitute` IS ONE OF
    `an offence under section 15, 16, 17, 18 or 63 of the Terrorism Act 2000`
    `an offence under paragraph 7(2) or (3) of Schedule 3 to the Anti-terrorism, Crime and Security Act 2001`
    `an offence under regulations 8 to 13, 25 or 26 of the ISIL (Da'esh) and Al-Qaida (United Nations Sanctions) (EU Exit) Regulations 2019 or regulations 11 to 16 of the Counter-Terrorism (International Sanctions) (EU Exit) Regulations 2019`
    `an offence under regulations 11 to 16 of the Counter-Terrorism (Sanctions) (EU Exit) Regulations 2019`
    `an offence under any other provision`

-- src:128 | “terrorist financing” means (except where the context otherwise requires) an act which constitutes an offence under—
-- src:129 | section 15 (fund-raising), 16 (use and possession), 17 (funding arrangements), 18 (money laundering) or 63 (terrorist finance: jurisdiction) of the Terrorism Act 2000 ;
-- src:130 | paragraph 7(2) or (3) of Schedule 3 (freezing orders: offences) to the Anti-terrorism, Crime and Security Act 2001 ;
-- src:131 | regulations 8 to 13, 25 or 26 of the ISIL (Da'esh) and Al-Qaida (United Nations Sanctions) (EU Exit) Regulations 2019 or regulations 11 to 16 of the Counter-Terrorism (International Sanctions) (EU Exit) Regulations 2019;; or
-- src:132 | any of regulations 11 to 16 of the Counter-Terrorism (Sanctions) (EU Exit) Regulations 2019;
@ref reg 3(1) "terrorist financing" (src:128-132)
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      offence IS A `reg 3(1) Offence an act may constitute`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 3(1) the act is terrorist financing` MEANS
    IF `the context otherwise requires`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(except where the context otherwise requires)"
    ELSE CONSIDER offence
        WHEN `an offence under section 15, 16, 17, 18 or 63 of the Terrorism Act 2000` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `an offence under paragraph 7(2) or (3) of Schedule 3 to the Anti-terrorism, Crime and Security Act 2001` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `an offence under regulations 8 to 13, 25 or 26 of the ISIL (Da'esh) and Al-Qaida (United Nations Sanctions) (EU Exit) Regulations 2019 or regulations 11 to 16 of the Counter-Terrorism (International Sanctions) (EU Exit) Regulations 2019` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `an offence under regulations 11 to 16 of the Counter-Terrorism (Sanctions) (EU Exit) Regulations 2019` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `an offence under any other provision` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means ... an act which constitutes an offence under—" followed by a closed list

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- “third country” and “UK regulated market”
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:134 | “third country” means a state other than the United Kingdom;
@ref reg 3(1) "third country" (src:134)
GIVEN `it is a state` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 3(1) the place is a third country` MEANS
    IF `it is a state` AND (NOT `it is the United Kingdom`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a state other than the United Kingdom"

-- src:139 | “UK regulated market” means a recognised investment exchange within the meaning of section 285(1)(a) of FSMA, which is not an overseas investment exchange within the meaning of section 313(1) of FSMA.
@ref reg 3(1) "UK regulated market" (src:139)
GIVEN `it is a recognised investment exchange within the meaning of section 285(1)(a) of FSMA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an overseas investment exchange within the meaning of section 313(1) of FSMA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 3(1) the market is a UK regulated market` MEANS
    IF `it is a recognised investment exchange within the meaning of section 285(1)(a) of FSMA` AND (NOT `it is an overseas investment exchange within the meaning of section 313(1) of FSMA`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a recognised investment exchange within the meaning of section 285(1)(a) of FSMA, which is not an overseas investment exchange within the meaning of section 313(1) of FSMA"


§ `reg 3(2) Rules of reading`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 3(2)(a) and (b): a sum in sterling, and its equivalent in another currency.
-- The representation: a sum is a NUMBER with a flag saying whether it is in sterling; the
-- exchange rate is the number of units of the other currency that buy one pound sterling at
-- the London closing rate for the previous working day (the rate is outside the text, so it is
-- an input).  "Working day" is defined only for Part 7A (reg 64B); reg 3(2)(b) does not define it.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:142 | (b) the equivalent in another currency on a particular day of a sum expressed in sterling is determined by converting the sum in sterling into its equivalent in ... that other currency using the London closing exchange rate for sterling and the relevant currency for the previous working day;
@ref reg 3(2)(b) (src:142)
GIVEN `the sum in sterling` IS A NUMBER
      `the London closing exchange rate for sterling and the other currency for the previous working day, in units of the other currency per pound sterling` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 3(2)(b) the equivalent in another currency of a sum in sterling` MEANS
    IF `the London closing exchange rate for sterling and the other currency for the previous working day, in units of the other currency per pound sterling` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST (`the sum in sterling` TIMES `the London closing exchange rate for sterling and the other currency for the previous working day, in units of the other currency per pound sterling`)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the rate is not in the text, and a rate that is not a positive number is no rate

-- src:141 | (a) references to an amount in sterling includes reference to an equivalent amount in any currency;
@ref reg 3(2)(a) (src:141)
GIVEN `the amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount is in sterling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sterling threshold` IS A NUMBER
      `the London closing exchange rate for the previous working day, in units of the other currency per pound sterling` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 3(2)(a) the amount is at least the sterling threshold` MEANS
    IF `the amount is in sterling`
    THEN JUST (`the amount` AT LEAST `the sterling threshold`)
    ELSE CONSIDER `reg 3(2)(b) the equivalent in another currency of a sum in sterling` `the sterling threshold` `the London closing exchange rate for the previous working day, in units of the other currency per pound sterling`
        WHEN JUST equivalent THEN JUST (`the amount` AT LEAST equivalent)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the exchange rate

-- src:141 | (a) references to an amount in sterling includes reference to an equivalent amount in any currency;
@ref reg 3(2)(a) (src:141)
GIVEN `the amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount is in sterling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sterling threshold` IS A NUMBER
      `the London closing exchange rate for the previous working day, in units of the other currency per pound sterling` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 3(2)(a) the amount exceeds the sterling threshold` MEANS
    IF `the amount is in sterling`
    THEN JUST (`the amount` GREATER THAN `the sterling threshold`)
    ELSE CONSIDER `reg 3(2)(b) the equivalent in another currency of a sum in sterling` `the sterling threshold` `the London closing exchange rate for the previous working day, in units of the other currency per pound sterling`
        WHEN JUST equivalent THEN JUST (`the amount` GREATER THAN equivalent)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the exchange rate

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 3(2)(c): "real property" includes heritable property in Scotland
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:143 | (c) references to “real property” include, in relation to Scotland, references to heritable property;
@ref reg 3(2)(c) (src:143)
GIVEN where IS A `Part of the United Kingdom`
      `the property is heritable property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 3(2)(c) the property is real property` MEANS
    CONSIDER where
    WHEN `Scotland` THEN
        IF `the property is heritable property`
        THEN JUST TRUE -- "references to “real property” include, in relation to Scotland, references to heritable property"
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include" does not close the list
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the paragraph adds heritable property for Scotland and says nothing about other property

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 3(2)(d), (e), (f): rules of reading that point
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:144 | (d) references to business being carried on in the United Kingdom, or a person carrying on business in the United Kingdom, are to be read in accordance with regulation 9;
@ref reg 3(2)(d) (src:144)
GIVETH A STRING
`reg 3(2)(d) references to carrying on business in the United Kingdom are read in accordance with` MEANS "regulation 9"

-- src:145 | (e) references to a person having a “qualifying relationship” with a PRA-authorised person, or with an authorised person are to be read in accordance with section 415B(4) of FSMA ;
@ref reg 3(2)(e) (src:145)
GIVETH A STRING
`reg 3(2)(e) a qualifying relationship is read in accordance with` MEANS "section 415B(4) of FSMA"

-- src:146 | (f) “parent undertaking” and “subsidiary undertaking” have the same meaning as in the Companies Acts (see section 1162 of and Schedule 7 to, the Companies Act 2006 (parent and subsidiary undertaking) ).
@ref reg 3(2)(f) (src:146)
GIVETH A STRING
`reg 3(2)(f) parent undertaking and subsidiary undertaking have the same meaning as in` MEANS "the Companies Acts (see section 1162 of and Schedule 7 to, the Companies Act 2006 (parent and subsidiary undertaking) )"

§ `reg 4 Meaning of business relationship`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 4(1): the definition
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:148 | (1) For the purpose of these Regulations, “business relationship” means a business, professional or commercial relationship between a relevant person and a customer, which—
-- src:149 | (a) arises out of the business of the relevant person, and
-- src:150 | (b) is expected by the relevant person, at the time when contact is established, to have an element of duration.
@ref reg 4(1) (src:148-150)
GIVEN `the relationship is a business, professional or commercial relationship between a relevant person and a customer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relationship arises out of the business of the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person expected, at the time when contact was established, that it would have an element of duration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 4(1) the relationship is a business relationship` MEANS
    IF `the relationship is a business, professional or commercial relationship between a relevant person and a customer`
       AND `the relationship arises out of the business of the relevant person`
       AND `the relevant person expected, at the time when contact was established, that it would have an element of duration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“business relationship” means a business, professional or commercial relationship between a relevant person and a customer, which— (a) arises out of the business of the relevant person, and (b) is expected by the relevant person, at the time when contact is established, to have an element of duration"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 4(2): trust or company services are a business relationship whatever the duration.
-- The services are those of reg 12(2)(a), (ab), (b) and (d), which is mlr1's range: asked as an input.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:151 | (2) A relationship where the relevant person is asked to provide one or more of the services described in regulation 12(2)(a), (ab), (b) or (d) is to be treated as a business relationship for the purpose of these Regulations, whether or not the relationship is otherwise expected to have an element of duration.
@ref reg 4(2) (src:151)
GIVEN `the relevant person is asked to provide one or more of the services described in regulation 12(2)(a), (ab), (b) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 4(2) the relationship is treated as a business relationship` MEANS
    IF `the relevant person is asked to provide one or more of the services described in regulation 12(2)(a), (ab), (b) or (d)`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- "is to be treated as a business relationship ... whether or not the relationship is otherwise expected to have an element of duration"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph treats a relationship of that kind as a business relationship and says nothing of any other

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 4(3): the estate agent and the purchaser
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:152 | (3) For the purposes of these Regulations, an estate agent is to be treated as entering into a business relationship with a purchaser (as well as with a seller), at the point when the purchaser's offer is accepted by the seller.
@ref reg 4(3) (src:152)
GIVEN `the kinds of relevant person` IS A LIST OF `Kind of relevant person`
      `the other party is the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller has accepted the purchaser's offer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 4(3) the estate agent is treated as entering into a business relationship with the purchaser` MEANS
    IF (elem `estate agent` `the kinds of relevant person`) AND `the other party is the purchaser` AND `the seller has accepted the purchaser's offer`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- "an estate agent is to be treated as entering into a business relationship with a purchaser (as well as with a seller), at the point when the purchaser's offer is accepted by the seller"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at the point when the purchaser's offer is accepted by the seller"; the paragraph says nothing before that point or of any other party

-- The point in time: the day the offer is accepted.  NOTHING until it is.
-- src:152 | (3) For the purposes of these Regulations, an estate agent is to be treated as entering into a business relationship with a purchaser (as well as with a seller), at the point when the purchaser's offer is accepted by the seller.
@ref reg 4(3) (src:152)
GIVEN `the kinds of relevant person` IS A LIST OF `Kind of relevant person`
      `the other party is the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the seller accepted the purchaser's offer` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`reg 4(3) the date on which the estate agent is treated as entering into a business relationship with the purchaser` MEANS
    IF (elem `estate agent` `the kinds of relevant person`) AND `the other party is the purchaser`
    THEN `the date the seller accepted the purchaser's offer`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of an estate agent and a purchaser

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 4(1) to (3) gathered by hand: one reader's convenience (ruling E1, option B as guidance
-- for gathering a legal effect's routes by hand only).  Each route above still answers on
-- its own (option C).  A route that is TRUE settles it; with none true, reg 4(1) says "means",
-- so the answer is no.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:148 | (1) For the purpose of these Regulations, “business relationship” means a business, professional or commercial relationship between a relevant person and a customer, which—
-- src:149 | (a) arises out of the business of the relevant person, and
-- src:150 | (b) is expected by the relevant person, at the time when contact is established, to have an element of duration.
-- src:151 | (2) A relationship where the relevant person is asked to provide one or more of the services described in regulation 12(2)(a), (ab), (b) or (d) is to be treated as a business relationship for the purpose of these Regulations, whether or not the relationship is otherwise expected to have an element of duration.
-- src:152 | (3) For the purposes of these Regulations, an estate agent is to be treated as entering into a business relationship with a purchaser (as well as with a seller), at the point when the purchaser's offer is accepted by the seller.
@ref reg 4(1) to (3) (src:148-152)
GIVEN `route (1) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `route (2) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `route (3) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` MEANS
    IF `route (1) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `route (2) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `route (3) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `route (1) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): reg 4(1) "means" a relationship of the described kind, and regs 4(2) and 4(3) add two routes; the described kind is absent and neither added route holds
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): route (1) has not been answered, so the paragraph cannot say no


§ `reg 5 Meaning of beneficial owner: bodies corporate or partnership`

-- The facts about ONE individual and ONE body corporate that reg 5(1) and (2) turn on.  The two
-- statutory tests that point into the Companies Act 2006 are borrowed (an Act outside the
-- sources) and are asked as plain BOOLEANs.  A share is a percentage from 0 to 100.
DECLARE `reg 5 Facts about an individual and a body corporate` HAS
    `exercises ultimate control over the management of the body corporate`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `percentage of the shares ultimately owned or controlled, directly or indirectly`  IS A NUMBER
    `percentage of the voting rights ultimately owned or controlled, directly or indirectly`  IS A NUMBER
    `satisfies one or more of the conditions in Part 1 of Schedule 1A to the Companies Act 2006`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the body corporate would be a subsidiary undertaking of the individual, if the individual was an undertaking, under section 1162 of the Companies Act 2006 read with Schedule 7 to that Act`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- reg 5(2): when an individual "controls" a body corporate, for reg 5(1)(c).
-- src:158 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(c), an individual controls a body corporate if—
-- src:159 | (a) the body corporate is a company or a limited liability partnership and that individual satisfies one or more of the conditions set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1A to the Companies Act 2006 (people with significant control over a company) ; or
-- src:160 | (b) the body corporate would be a subsidiary undertaking of the individual (if the individual was an undertaking) under section 1162 (parent and subsidiary undertakings) of the Companies Act 2006 read with Schedule 7 to that Act.
@ref reg 5(2) (src:158-160)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of customer`
      facts IS A `reg 5 Facts about an individual and a body corporate`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 5(2) the individual controls the body corporate` MEANS
    IF ((form EQUALS `a company`) OR (form EQUALS `a limited liability partnership`))
       AND facts's `satisfies one or more of the conditions in Part 1 of Schedule 1A to the Companies Act 2006`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF facts's `the body corporate would be a subsidiary undertaking of the individual, if the individual was an undertaking, under section 1162 of the Companies Act 2006 read with Schedule 7 to that Act`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an individual controls a body corporate if" (a) ... or (b) ...; an "if" read as the text's no (Marginal readings, (a))

-- reg 5(1): the individual is a beneficial owner of a body corporate that is not a listed company.
-- src:154 | (1) In these Regulations, “beneficial owner”, in relation to a body corporate which is not a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market, means—
-- src:155 | (a) any individual who exercises ultimate control over the management of the body corporate;
-- src:156 | (b) any individual who ultimately owns or controls (in each case whether directly or indirectly), including through bearer share holdings or by other means, more than 25% of the shares or voting rights in the body corporate; or
-- src:157 | (c) an individual who controls the body corporate.
@ref reg 5(1) (src:154-157)
GIVEN customer IS A Customer
      facts IS A `reg 5 Facts about an individual and a body corporate`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 5(1) the individual is a beneficial owner of the body corporate` MEANS
    CONSIDER customer's `form of the customer`
    WHEN `a company` THEN
        IF customer's `securities listed on a regulated market`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (1) speaks of a body corporate "which is not a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market"; where a listed company then falls is not said (fork: A listed company)
        ELSE `limbs (a) to (c)`
    WHEN `a limited liability partnership` THEN `limbs (a) to (c)`
    WHEN `a body corporate of another kind` THEN `limbs (a) to (c)`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (1) speaks of a body corporate; the other forms are the business of reg 5(3) and reg 6
    WHERE
        `limbs (a) to (c)` MEANS
            IF facts's `exercises ultimate control over the management of the body corporate`
               OR (facts's `percentage of the shares ultimately owned or controlled, directly or indirectly` GREATER THAN 25)
               OR (facts's `percentage of the voting rights ultimately owned or controlled, directly or indirectly` GREATER THAN 25)
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE CONSIDER `reg 5(2) the individual controls the body corporate` (customer's `form of the customer`) facts
                WHEN JUST controls THEN
                    IF controls
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“beneficial owner”, in relation to a body corporate ..., means— (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) an individual who controls the body corporate"
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): reg 5(2) gave no answer

-- reg 5(3): a partnership other than a limited liability partnership.
DECLARE `reg 5 Facts about an individual and a partnership` HAS
    `percentage of the capital ultimately entitled to or controlled, directly or indirectly`  IS A NUMBER
    `percentage of the profits ultimately entitled to or controlled, directly or indirectly`  IS A NUMBER
    `percentage of the voting rights ultimately entitled to or controlled, directly or indirectly`  IS A NUMBER
    `satisfies one or more of the conditions in Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the Scottish Partnerships (Register of People with Significant Control) Regulations 2017`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `otherwise exercises ultimate control over the management of the partnership`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:161 | (3) In these Regulations, “beneficial owner”, in relation to a partnership (other than a limited liability partnership), means any individual who—
-- src:162 | (a) ultimately is entitled to or controls (in each case whether directly or indirectly) more than 25% share of the capital or profits of the partnership or more than 25% of the voting rights in the partnership;
-- src:163 | (b) satisfies one or more the conditions set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the Scottish Partnerships (Register of People with Significant Control) Regulations 2017 (references to people with significant control over an eligible Scottish partnership) ; or
-- src:164 | (c) otherwise exercises ultimate control over the management of the partnership.
@ref reg 5(3) (src:161-164)
GIVEN customer IS A Customer
      facts IS A `reg 5 Facts about an individual and a partnership`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 5(3) the individual is a beneficial owner of the partnership` MEANS
    IF customer's `form of the customer` EQUALS `a partnership other than a limited liability partnership`
    THEN
        IF (facts's `percentage of the capital ultimately entitled to or controlled, directly or indirectly` GREATER THAN 25)
           OR (facts's `percentage of the profits ultimately entitled to or controlled, directly or indirectly` GREATER THAN 25)
           OR (facts's `percentage of the voting rights ultimately entitled to or controlled, directly or indirectly` GREATER THAN 25)
           OR facts's `satisfies one or more of the conditions in Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the Scottish Partnerships (Register of People with Significant Control) Regulations 2017`
           OR facts's `otherwise exercises ultimate control over the management of the partnership`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“beneficial owner”, in relation to a partnership (other than a limited liability partnership), means any individual who— (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) otherwise exercises ultimate control over the management of the partnership"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (3) speaks of a partnership other than a limited liability partnership

-- reg 5(4): "limited liability partnership" is a borrowed term.
-- src:165 | (4) In this regulation “limited liability partnership” has the meaning given by the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000 .
@ref reg 5(4) (src:165)
GIVETH A STRING
`reg 5(4) limited liability partnership is given by` MEANS "the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000"

§ `reg 6 Meaning of beneficial owner: trusts, similar arrangements and others`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 6(2): "control" of a trust is a power of one of five kinds
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:173 | (2) In paragraph (1)(e), “control” means a power (whether exercisable alone, jointly with another person or with the consent of another person) under the trust instrument or by law to—
-- src:174 | (a) dispose of, advance, lend, invest, pay or apply trust property;
-- src:175 | (b) vary or terminate the trust;
-- src:176 | (c) add or remove a person as a beneficiary or to or from a class of beneficiaries;
-- src:177 | (d) appoint or remove trustees or give another individual control over the trust;
-- src:178 | (e) direct, withhold consent to or veto the exercise of a power mentioned in sub-paragraphs (a) to (d).
@ref reg 6(2) (src:173-178)
GIVEN `the individual holds a power under the trust instrument or by law, whether exercisable alone, jointly with another person or with the consent of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is a power to dispose of, advance, lend, invest, pay or apply trust property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is a power to vary or terminate the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is a power to add or remove a person as a beneficiary or to or from a class of beneficiaries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is a power to appoint or remove trustees or give another individual control over the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is a power to direct, withhold consent to or veto the exercise of a power mentioned in sub-paragraphs (a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 6(2) the power is control over the trust` MEANS
    IF `the individual holds a power under the trust instrument or by law, whether exercisable alone, jointly with another person or with the consent of another person`
       AND (   `the power is a power to dispose of, advance, lend, invest, pay or apply trust property`
            OR `the power is a power to vary or terminate the trust`
            OR `the power is a power to add or remove a person as a beneficiary or to or from a class of beneficiaries`
            OR `the power is a power to appoint or remove trustees or give another individual control over the trust`
            OR `the power is a power to direct, withhold consent to or veto the exercise of a power mentioned in sub-paragraphs (a) to (d)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“control” means a power ... under the trust instrument or by law to— (a) ... (e) ..."

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 6(4)(b): an individual does not have control solely as a result of one of four things.
-- The answer is to the question "does the individual have control over the trust?"
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:182 | (b) an individual (“P”) does not have control solely as a result of—
-- src:183 | (i) P's consent being required in accordance with section 32(1)(c) (power of advancement) of the Trustee Act 1925 ;
-- src:184 | (ii) any discretion delegated to P under section 34 (power of investment and delegation) of the Pensions Act 1995 ;
-- src:185 | (iii) the power to give a direction conferred on P by section 19(2) (appointment and retirement of trustee at instance of beneficiaries) of the Trusts of Land and Appointment of Trustees Act 1996 ; or
-- src:186 | (iv) the power exercisable collectively at common law to vary or extinguish a trust where the beneficiaries under the trust are of full age and capacity and (taken together) absolutely entitled to the property subject to the trust (or, in Scotland, have a full and unqualified right to the fee).
@ref reg 6(4)(b) (src:182-186)
GIVEN `the only basis of the power is P's consent being required in accordance with section 32(1)(c) (power of advancement) of the Trustee Act 1925` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only basis of the power is a discretion delegated to P under section 34 (power of investment and delegation) of the Pensions Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only basis of the power is the power to give a direction conferred on P by section 19(2) (appointment and retirement of trustee at instance of beneficiaries) of the Trusts of Land and Appointment of Trustees Act 1996` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only basis of the power is the power exercisable collectively at common law to vary or extinguish a trust where the beneficiaries under the trust are of full age and capacity and (taken together) absolutely entitled to the property subject to the trust (or, in Scotland, have a full and unqualified right to the fee)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 6(4)(b) the individual has control over the trust, given the four exclusions` MEANS
    IF `the only basis of the power is P's consent being required in accordance with section 32(1)(c) (power of advancement) of the Trustee Act 1925`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an individual (“P”) does not have control solely as a result of— (i) P's consent being required in accordance with section 32(1)(c)" (Marginal readings, (a): a flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE IF `the only basis of the power is a discretion delegated to P under section 34 (power of investment and delegation) of the Pensions Act 1995`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) any discretion delegated to P under section 34 (power of investment and delegation) of the Pensions Act 1995" (Marginal readings, (a))
        ELSE IF `the only basis of the power is the power to give a direction conferred on P by section 19(2) (appointment and retirement of trustee at instance of beneficiaries) of the Trusts of Land and Appointment of Trustees Act 1996`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(iii) the power to give a direction conferred on P by section 19(2)" (Marginal readings, (a))
            ELSE IF `the only basis of the power is the power exercisable collectively at common law to vary or extinguish a trust where the beneficiaries under the trust are of full age and capacity and (taken together) absolutely entitled to the property subject to the trust (or, in Scotland, have a full and unqualified right to the fee)`
                THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(iv) the power exercisable collectively at common law to vary or extinguish a trust" (Marginal readings, (a))
                ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says what is not control; it does not say that anything else is

-- Control, with reg 6(4)(b) applied to reg 6(2) (the two gathered by hand, ruling E1 option B).
-- src:173 | (2) In paragraph (1)(e), “control” means a power (whether exercisable alone, jointly with another person or with the consent of another person) under the trust instrument or by law to—
-- src:174 | (a) dispose of, advance, lend, invest, pay or apply trust property;
-- src:175 | (b) vary or terminate the trust;
-- src:176 | (c) add or remove a person as a beneficiary or to or from a class of beneficiaries;
-- src:177 | (d) appoint or remove trustees or give another individual control over the trust;
-- src:178 | (e) direct, withhold consent to or veto the exercise of a power mentioned in sub-paragraphs (a) to (d).
-- src:182 | (b) an individual (“P”) does not have control solely as a result of—
-- src:183 | (i) P's consent being required in accordance with section 32(1)(c) (power of advancement) of the Trustee Act 1925 ;
-- src:184 | (ii) any discretion delegated to P under section 34 (power of investment and delegation) of the Pensions Act 1995 ;
-- src:185 | (iii) the power to give a direction conferred on P by section 19(2) (appointment and retirement of trustee at instance of beneficiaries) of the Trusts of Land and Appointment of Trustees Act 1996 ; or
-- src:186 | (iv) the power exercisable collectively at common law to vary or extinguish a trust where the beneficiaries under the trust are of full age and capacity and (taken together) absolutely entitled to the property subject to the trust (or, in Scotland, have a full and unqualified right to the fee).
@ref reg 6(2) and (4)(b) (src:173-178) (src:182-186)
GIVEN `the answer under regulation 6(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under regulation 6(4)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 6(2) and (4)(b) the individual has control over the trust` MEANS
    IF `the answer under regulation 6(4)(b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): reg 6(4)(b), "does not have control solely as a result of" (Marginal readings, (a))
    ELSE `the answer under regulation 6(2)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 6(1): a trust
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DECLARE `reg 6(1) Position in relation to a trust` IS ONE OF
    `the settlor`
    `a trustee`
    `a beneficiary`
    `a member of the class of persons in whose main interest the trust is set up, or operates`
    `an individual who has control over the trust`
    `some other position in relation to the trust`

-- src:167 | (1) In these Regulations, “beneficial owner”, in relation to a trust, means each of the following—
-- src:168 | (a) the settlor;
-- src:169 | (b) the trustees;
-- src:170 | (c) the beneficiaries;
-- src:171 | (d) where the individuals (or some of the individuals) benefiting from the trust have not been determined, the class of persons in whose main interest the trust is set up, or operates;
-- src:172 | (e) any individual who has control over the trust.
@ref reg 6(1) (src:167-172)
GIVEN position IS A `reg 6(1) Position in relation to a trust`
      `the individuals (or some of the individuals) benefiting from the trust have not been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has control over the trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 6(1) the person is a beneficial owner of the trust` MEANS
    CONSIDER position
    WHEN `the settlor` THEN JUST TRUE -- (a)
    WHEN `a trustee` THEN JUST TRUE -- (b)
    WHEN `a beneficiary` THEN JUST TRUE -- (c)
    WHEN `a member of the class of persons in whose main interest the trust is set up, or operates` THEN
        IF `the individuals (or some of the individuals) benefiting from the trust have not been determined`
        THEN JUST TRUE -- (d)
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the individuals (or some of the individuals) benefiting from the trust have not been determined" (Marginal readings, (b))
    WHEN `an individual who has control over the trust` THEN `the individual has control over the trust` -- (e); the answer of reg 6(2) and (4)(b), passed through whole
    WHEN `some other position in relation to the trust` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“beneficial owner”, in relation to a trust, means each of the following"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 6(3): a foundation or other legal arrangement similar to a trust
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:179 | (3) In these Regulations, “beneficial owner”, in relation to a foundation or other legal arrangement similar to a trust, means those individuals who hold equivalent or similar positions to those set out in paragraph (1).
@ref reg 6(3) (src:179)
GIVEN `the individual holds an equivalent or similar position to one set out in paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 6(3) the individual is a beneficial owner of the foundation or other legal arrangement` MEANS
    IF `the individual holds an equivalent or similar position to one set out in paragraph (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means those individuals who hold equivalent or similar positions to those set out in paragraph (1)"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 6(4)(a) and (5): a body corporate's interest or control counts for its beneficial owner
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:181 | (a) where an individual is the beneficial owner of a body corporate which is entitled to a specified interest in the capital of the trust property or which has control over the trust, the individual is to be regarded as entitled to the interest or having control over the trust; and
@ref reg 6(4)(a) (src:181)
GIVEN `the individual is the beneficial owner of a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate is entitled to a specified interest in the capital of the trust property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate has control over the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 6(4)(a) the individual is regarded as entitled to the interest or having control over the trust` MEANS
    IF `the individual is the beneficial owner of a body corporate` AND (`the body corporate is entitled to a specified interest in the capital of the trust property` OR `the body corporate has control over the trust`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where an individual is the beneficial owner of a body corporate which is entitled to a specified interest ... or which has control over the trust"

-- src:187 | (5) For the purposes of paragraph (4), “specified interest” means a vested interest which is—
-- src:188 | (a) in possession or in remainder or reversion (or in Scotland, in fee); and
-- src:189 | (b) defeasible or indefeasible.
@ref reg 6(5) (src:187-189)
GIVEN `the interest is a vested interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest is in possession or in remainder or reversion (or in Scotland, in fee)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest is defeasible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest is indefeasible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 6(5) the interest is a specified interest` MEANS
    IF `the interest is a vested interest`
       AND `the interest is in possession or in remainder or reversion (or in Scotland, in fee)`
       AND (`the interest is defeasible` OR `the interest is indefeasible`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“specified interest” means a vested interest which is— (a) in possession or in remainder or reversion (or in Scotland, in fee); and (b) defeasible or indefeasible"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 6(6): the estate of a deceased person in the course of administration
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:190 | (6) In these Regulations, “beneficial owner”, in relation to an estate of a deceased person in the course of administration, means—
-- src:191 | (a) in England and Wales and Northern Ireland, the executor, original or by representation, or administrator for the time being of a deceased person;
-- src:192 | (b) in Scotland, the executor for the purposes of the Executors (Scotland) Act 1900 .
@ref reg 6(6) (src:190-192)
GIVEN where IS A `Part of the United Kingdom`
      `the person is the executor, original or by representation, or the administrator for the time being, of the deceased person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the executor for the purposes of the Executors (Scotland) Act 1900` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 6(6) the person is a beneficial owner of the estate` MEANS
    CONSIDER where
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN
        IF `the person is the executor, original or by representation, or the administrator for the time being, of the deceased person`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to an estate of a deceased person in the course of administration, means— (a) in England and Wales and Northern Ireland, the executor, original or by representation, or administrator for the time being"
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN
        IF `the person is the executor, original or by representation, or the administrator for the time being, of the deceased person`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) in England and Wales and Northern Ireland, the executor, original or by representation, or administrator for the time being"
    WHEN `Scotland` THEN
        IF `the person is the executor for the purposes of the Executors (Scotland) Act 1900`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in Scotland, the executor for the purposes of the Executors (Scotland) Act 1900"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 6(7) and (8): a legal entity or arrangement outside reg 5 and reg 6(1), (3) and (6)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DECLARE `reg 6(7) Position in relation to a legal entity or legal arrangement` IS ONE OF
    `an individual who benefits from the property of the entity or arrangement`
    `a member of the class of persons in whose main interest the entity or arrangement is set up or operates`
    `an individual who exercises control over the property of the entity or arrangement`
    `some other position in relation to the entity or arrangement`

-- src:193 | (7) In these Regulations, “beneficial owner”, in relation to a legal entity or legal arrangement which does not fall within regulation 5 or paragraphs (1), (3) or (6) of this regulation, means—
-- src:194 | (a) any individual who benefits from the property of the entity or arrangement;
-- src:195 | (b) where the individuals who benefit from the entity or arrangement have yet to be determined, the class of persons in whose main interest the entity or arrangement is set up or operates;
-- src:196 | (c) any individual who exercises control over the property of the entity or arrangement.
@ref reg 6(7) (src:193-196)
GIVEN position IS A `reg 6(7) Position in relation to a legal entity or legal arrangement`
      `the individuals who benefit from the entity or arrangement have yet to be determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 6(7) the person is a beneficial owner of the legal entity or arrangement` MEANS
    CONSIDER position
    WHEN `an individual who benefits from the property of the entity or arrangement` THEN JUST TRUE -- (a)
    WHEN `a member of the class of persons in whose main interest the entity or arrangement is set up or operates` THEN
        IF `the individuals who benefit from the entity or arrangement have yet to be determined`
        THEN JUST TRUE -- (b)
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the individuals who benefit from the entity or arrangement have yet to be determined" (Marginal readings, (b))
    WHEN `an individual who exercises control over the property of the entity or arrangement` THEN JUST TRUE -- (c)
    WHEN `some other position in relation to the entity or arrangement` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“beneficial owner”, in relation to a legal entity or legal arrangement which does not fall within regulation 5 or paragraphs (1), (3) or (6) of this regulation, means"

-- src:197 | (8) For the purposes of paragraph (7), where an individual is the beneficial owner of a body corporate which benefits from or exercises control over the property of the entity or arrangement, the individual is to be regarded as benefiting from or exercising control over the property of the entity or arrangement.
@ref reg 6(8) (src:197)
GIVEN `the individual is the beneficial owner of a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate benefits from the property of the entity or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate exercises control over the property of the entity or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 6(8) the individual is regarded as benefiting from or exercising control over the property` MEANS
    IF `the individual is the beneficial owner of a body corporate` AND (`the body corporate benefits from the property of the entity or arrangement` OR `the body corporate exercises control over the property of the entity or arrangement`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where an individual is the beneficial owner of a body corporate which benefits from or exercises control over the property"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 6(9): any other case
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:198 | (9) In these Regulations, “beneficial owner”, in any other case, means the individual who ultimately owns or controls the entity or arrangement or on whose behalf a transaction is being conducted.
@ref reg 6(9) (src:198)
GIVEN `the individual ultimately owns or controls the entity or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a transaction is being conducted on behalf of the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 6(9) the individual is a beneficial owner in any other case` MEANS
    IF `the individual ultimately owns or controls the entity or arrangement` OR `a transaction is being conducted on behalf of the individual`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“beneficial owner”, in any other case, means the individual who ultimately owns or controls the entity or arrangement or on whose behalf a transaction is being conducted"

-- reg 6(7) and reg 6(9) both speak of a legal entity that is not a body corporate, a partnership,
-- a trust or an estate (reg 3(1) sends "any other case" to reg 6(9); reg 6(7) speaks of an entity
-- outside reg 5 and reg 6(1), (3) and (6)).  The text does not say which governs (fork: 6(7)
-- against 6(9)).  Gathered by hand (ruling E1 option B): where they agree the answer is that
-- answer; where only reg 6(7) says yes, the text does not choose.
-- src:193 | (7) In these Regulations, “beneficial owner”, in relation to a legal entity or legal arrangement which does not fall within regulation 5 or paragraphs (1), (3) or (6) of this regulation, means—
-- src:194 | (a) any individual who benefits from the property of the entity or arrangement;
-- src:195 | (b) where the individuals who benefit from the entity or arrangement have yet to be determined, the class of persons in whose main interest the entity or arrangement is set up or operates;
-- src:196 | (c) any individual who exercises control over the property of the entity or arrangement.
-- src:198 | (9) In these Regulations, “beneficial owner”, in any other case, means the individual who ultimately owns or controls the entity or arrangement or on whose behalf a transaction is being conducted.
@ref reg 6(7) and (9) (src:193-196) (src:198)
GIVEN `the answer under regulation 6(7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under regulation 6(9)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 6(7) and (9) the individual is a beneficial owner of an entity outside regulation 5 and regulation 6(1), (3) and (6)` MEANS
    IF `the answer under regulation 6(9)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE -- reg 6(9) says yes and so does every reading
    ELSE IF `the answer under regulation 6(7)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): reg 6(7) says yes and reg 6(9) says no; the text does not say which governs the entity
        ELSE IF `the answer under regulation 6(7)` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `the answer under regulation 6(9)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): both "means" definitions say no
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): at least one of the two has not been answered


§ `reg 7 Supervisory authorities`

-- The facts about the relevant person that reg 7(1) sorts on.  Most are borrowed (FSMA, the
-- Payment Services Regulations, the Electronic Money Regulations) and are asked as plain
-- facts; whether the person is a credit institution, an estate agent and so on is the output
-- of regs 10 to 14A (mlr1's rows) and arrives in `kinds of relevant person`.
DECLARE `reg 7 Facts about the relevant person` HAS
    `kinds of relevant person`                                   IS A LIST OF `Kind of relevant person`
    `an authorised person`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `a money service business`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `an excluded money service business`                         IS A BOOLEAN -- reg 7(5)
    `an Annex 1 financial institution`                           IS A BOOLEAN -- reg 55(2), mlr3's row
    `an electronic money institution`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `a credit union in Northern Ireland`                         IS A BOOLEAN -- reg 7(7)
    `a recognised investment exchange within the meaning of section 285 of FSMA`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a bill payment service provider`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `professional bodies of which it is a member, or by which it is regulated or supervised`  IS A LIST OF `Professional body`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 7(1)(a) to (d): the four lists.  Each answers a plain question of class membership
-- (BOOLEAN); it is not an answer the Regulations give about a person outside the lists.  The
-- paragraph as a whole answers below, with NOTHING where no list takes the person.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:201 | (a) the FCA is the supervisory authority for—
-- src:202 | (i) credit and financial institutions (including money service businesses) which are authorised persons but not excluded money service businesses;
-- src:203 | (ii) trust or company service providers which are authorised persons;
-- src:204 | (iii) Annex 1 financial institutions;
-- src:205 | (iv) electronic money institutions;
-- src:206 | (v) auction platforms;
-- src:207 | (vi) credit unions in Northern Ireland;
-- src:208 | (vii) recognised investment exchanges within the meaning of section 285 of FSMA (exemption for recognised investment exchanges , clearing houses and central securities depositories);
-- src:209 | (viii) cryptoasset exchange providers;
-- src:210 | (ix) custodian wallet providers;
@ref reg 7(1)(a) (src:201-210)
GIVEN facts IS A `reg 7 Facts about the relevant person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 7(1)(a) the relevant person is within a class the FCA supervises` MEANS
        (    (   `has the kind` `credit institution`
              OR `has the kind` `financial institution`
              OR facts's `a money service business`)
         AND facts's `an authorised person`
         AND (NOT (facts's `an excluded money service business`)))                  -- (i) credit and financial institutions (including money service businesses) which are authorised persons but not excluded money service businesses
    OR  (`has the kind` `trust or company service provider` AND facts's `an authorised person`)  -- (ii)
    OR  facts's `an Annex 1 financial institution`                                    -- (iii)
    OR  facts's `an electronic money institution`                                     -- (iv)
    OR  `has the kind` `auction platform`                                             -- (v)
    OR  facts's `a credit union in Northern Ireland`                                  -- (vi)
    OR  facts's `a recognised investment exchange within the meaning of section 285 of FSMA`  -- (vii)
    OR  `has the kind` `cryptoasset exchange provider`                                -- (viii)
    OR  `has the kind` `custodian wallet provider`                                    -- (ix)
    WHERE
        `has the kind` k MEANS elem k (facts's `kinds of relevant person`)

-- src:211 | (b) each of the professional bodies listed in Schedule 1 is the supervisory authority for relevant persons who are members of it, or regulated or supervised by it;
@ref reg 7(1)(b) (src:211)
GIVEN facts IS A `reg 7 Facts about the relevant person`
GIVETH A LIST OF Authority
`reg 7(1)(b) the professional bodies that are supervisory authorities for the relevant person` MEANS
    map (GIVEN body YIELD `a professional body listed in Schedule 1` body) (facts's `professional bodies of which it is a member, or by which it is regulated or supervised`)

-- src:212 | (c) the Commissioners are the supervisory authority for—
-- src:213 | (i) high value dealers;
-- src:214 | (ii) money service businesses which are not supervised by the FCA;
-- src:215 | (iii) trust or company service providers which are not supervised by the FCA or one of the professional bodies listed in Schedule 1;
-- src:216 | (iv) auditors, external accountants and tax advisers who are not supervised by one of the professional bodies listed in Schedule 1;
-- src:217 | (v) bill payment service providers which are not supervised by the FCA;
-- src:218 | (vi) telecommunication, digital and IT payment service providers which are not supervised by the FCA;
-- src:219 | (vii) estate agents and letting agents which are not supervised by one of the professional bodies listed in Schedule 1;
-- src:220 | (viii) art market participants;
@ref reg 7(1)(c) (src:212-220)
GIVEN facts IS A `reg 7 Facts about the relevant person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 7(1)(c) the relevant person is within a class the Commissioners supervise` MEANS
        `has the kind` `high value dealer`                                                          -- (i)
    OR  (facts's `a money service business` AND (NOT `supervised by the FCA`))                    -- (ii) money service businesses which are not supervised by the FCA
    OR  (`has the kind` `trust or company service provider` AND (NOT `supervised by the FCA`) AND (NOT `supervised by a professional body`))  -- (iii)
    OR  ((   `has the kind` `auditor`
          OR `has the kind` `external accountant`
          OR `has the kind` `tax adviser`)
         AND (NOT `supervised by a professional body`))                                           -- (iv)
    OR  (facts's `a bill payment service provider` AND (NOT `supervised by the FCA`))             -- (v)
    OR  (facts's `a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider` AND (NOT `supervised by the FCA`))  -- (vi)
    OR  ((   `has the kind` `estate agent`
          OR `has the kind` `letting agent`)
         AND (NOT `supervised by a professional body`))                                           -- (vii)
    OR  `has the kind` `art market participant`                                                   -- (viii)
    WHERE
        `has the kind` k MEANS elem k (facts's `kinds of relevant person`)
        `supervised by the FCA` MEANS `reg 7(1)(a) the relevant person is within a class the FCA supervises` facts
        `supervised by a professional body` MEANS NOT (null (facts's `professional bodies of which it is a member, or by which it is regulated or supervised`))

-- src:221 | (d) the Gambling Commission is the supervisory authority for casinos.
@ref reg 7(1)(d) (src:221)
GIVEN facts IS A `reg 7 Facts about the relevant person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 7(1)(d) the relevant person is within a class the Gambling Commission supervises` MEANS
    elem `casino` (facts's `kinds of relevant person`)

-- reg 7(1) as a whole.  The authorities are all those that apply: a person can have more than
-- one (reg 7(2) then lets them agree that one acts).  The paragraph is "subject to paragraph (2)".
-- src:200 | (1) Subject to paragraph (2), the following bodies are supervisory authorities in relation to relevant persons—
@ref reg 7(1) (src:200)
GIVEN facts IS A `reg 7 Facts about the relevant person`
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Authority)
`reg 7(1) the supervisory authorities of the relevant person` MEANS
    IF null `all the authorities`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): reg 7(1) says who supervises the persons it lists and says nothing of a person it does not list
    ELSE JUST `all the authorities`
    WHERE
        `all the authorities` MEANS
            append `the FCA, if listed`
                (append (`reg 7(1)(b) the professional bodies that are supervisory authorities for the relevant person` facts)
                    (append `the Commissioners, if listed` `the Gambling Commission, if listed`))
        `the FCA, if listed` MEANS
            IF `reg 7(1)(a) the relevant person is within a class the FCA supervises` facts
            THEN LIST `the Financial Conduct Authority`
            ELSE EMPTY
        `the Commissioners, if listed` MEANS
            IF `reg 7(1)(c) the relevant person is within a class the Commissioners supervise` facts
            THEN LIST `the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs`
            ELSE EMPTY
        `the Gambling Commission, if listed` MEANS
            IF `reg 7(1)(d) the relevant person is within a class the Gambling Commission supervises` facts
            THEN LIST `the Gambling Commission`
            ELSE EMPTY

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 7(2): an agreement that one authority acts
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:222 | (2) Where under paragraph (1), there is more than one supervisory authority for a relevant person, the supervisory authorities may agree that one of them will act as the supervisory authority for that person.
@ref reg 7(2) (src:222)
GIVEN authorities IS A LIST OF Authority
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 7(2) the supervisory authorities may agree that one of them acts as the supervisory authority` MEANS
    CONSIDER authorities
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where ... there is more than one supervisory authority"
    WHEN authority FOLLOWED BY EMPTY THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where ... there is more than one supervisory authority"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- "the supervisory authorities may agree that one of them will act as the supervisory authority for that person"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 7(3): what the authority that agreed to act must do
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:223 | (3) Where there has been an agreement under paragraph (2), the authority which has agreed to act as the supervisory authority must notify the relevant person or publish the agreement in such manner as it considers appropriate.
@ref reg 7(3) (src:223)
GIVEN `there has been an agreement under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority which has agreed to act has notified the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority which has agreed to act has published the agreement in such manner as it considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 7(3) the authority which agreed to act has notified the relevant person or published the agreement` MEANS
    IF NOT `there has been an agreement under paragraph (2)`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where there has been an agreement under paragraph (2)"
    ELSE IF `the authority which has agreed to act has notified the relevant person` OR `the authority which has agreed to act has published the agreement in such manner as it considers appropriate`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must notify the relevant person or publish the agreement" read as a flat duty, so that neither having happened is the text's no (Marginal readings, (c))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 7(4): no agreement, so the authorities must co-operate
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:224 | (4) Where there has not been an agreement under paragraph (2), the supervisory authorities for a relevant person must co-operate in the performance of their functions under these Regulations.
@ref reg 7(4) (src:224)
GIVEN `there has been an agreement under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is more than one supervisory authority for the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 7(4) the supervisory authorities for the relevant person must co-operate in the performance of their functions` MEANS
    IF (NOT `there has been an agreement under paragraph (2)`) AND `there is more than one supervisory authority for the relevant person`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- "must co-operate in the performance of their functions under these Regulations"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where there has not been an agreement under paragraph (2)"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 7(5) and (6): the excluded money service business
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:225 | (5) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(a)(i), a money service business is an “excluded money service business” if it is an authorised person who has permission under FSMA which relates to or is connected with a contract of the kind mentioned in paragraph 23 or 23B of Schedule 2 to that Act (credit agreements and contracts for hire of goods) but does not have permission to carry on any other kind of regulated activity.
@ref reg 7(5) (src:225)
GIVEN `the person is a money service business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has permission under FSMA which relates to or is connected with a contract of the kind mentioned in paragraph 23 or 23B of Schedule 2 to that Act (credit agreements and contracts for hire of goods)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has permission to carry on any other kind of regulated activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 7(5) the money service business is an excluded money service business` MEANS
    IF `the person is a money service business`
       AND `the person is an authorised person`
       AND `the person has permission under FSMA which relates to or is connected with a contract of the kind mentioned in paragraph 23 or 23B of Schedule 2 to that Act (credit agreements and contracts for hire of goods)`
       AND (NOT `the person has permission to carry on any other kind of regulated activity`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a money service business is an “excluded money service business” if it is an authorised person who has permission ... but does not have permission to carry on any other kind of regulated activity"; an "if" read as the text's no (Marginal readings, (a))

-- src:226 | (6) Paragraph (5) must be read with—
-- src:227 | (a) section 22 of FSMA (regulated activities) ;
-- src:228 | (b) any relevant order under that section; and
-- src:229 | (c) Schedule 2 to that Act.
@ref reg 7(6) (src:226-229)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`reg 7(6) paragraph (5) must be read with` MEANS
    LIST "section 22 of FSMA (regulated activities)"
       , "any relevant order under that section"
       , "Schedule 2 to that Act"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- reg 7(7): a credit union in Northern Ireland
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- src:230 | (7) For the purposes of paragraph (1), a credit union in Northern Ireland is a credit union which is—
-- src:231 | (a) registered under regulation 3 of the Credit Unions (Northern Ireland) Order 1985 (registration) and it is an authorised person; or
-- src:232 | (b) registered under Part 2 of the Industrial and Provident Societies Act (Northern Ireland) 1969 (registered societies) as a credit union and it is an authorised person.
@ref reg 7(7) (src:230-232)
GIVEN `the credit union is registered under regulation 3 of the Credit Unions (Northern Ireland) Order 1985 (registration)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the credit union is registered under Part 2 of the Industrial and Provident Societies Act (Northern Ireland) 1969 (registered societies) as a credit union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the credit union is an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 7(7) the credit union is a credit union in Northern Ireland` MEANS
    IF (`the credit union is registered under regulation 3 of the Credit Unions (Northern Ireland) Order 1985 (registration)` OR `the credit union is registered under Part 2 of the Industrial and Provident Societies Act (Northern Ireland) 1969 (registered societies) as a credit union`)
       AND `the credit union is an authorised person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a credit union in Northern Ireland is a credit union which is— (a) registered under regulation 3 ... and it is an authorised person; or (b) registered under Part 2 ... as a credit union and it is an authorised person" (Marginal readings, (a): "is a credit union which is", a definition by "is")
